# 11. IMPORTANT IDEAS WORTH PRESERVING

These are observations and ideas from the founder that deserve to remain part of the project's history.

### A. Don't spend forever reinventing existing technology.

The founder has expressed concern about spending enormous amounts of time rebuilding things that already exist.

We should investigate existing tools, engines, libraries, and systems before creating replacements.

Build custom technology when it provides meaningful value.

### B. AI collaboration has enormous potential.

One of the biggest discoveries has been seeing how multiple AI assistants can turn a relatively simple task into a much deeper development discussion.

This is a central motivation behind Creation Station.

### C. Preserve the ability to experiment.

The environment should make experimentation easier, not more complicated.

We should avoid building so much infrastructure that we spend all our time maintaining infrastructure.

### D. Keep the work accessible.

Important knowledge should exist outside individual conversations.

Source code should remain visible.

Documentation should be portable.

The founder should understand and control the environment.

### E. Don't lose the history.

The original pinball project demonstrated how much valuable knowledge can accumulate during development.

Even when a particular implementation is abandoned, the knowledge gained should remain available.

### F. Let the project grow.

Creation Station should be allowed to become something larger than its original concept.

New discoveries should be incorporated without losing the original direction.

